course: dictionary
lesson: 5143
title: Brand names and tablets
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An iPad is a tablet computer made by the company Apple. You touch its screen with your finger, because it has no keyboard. «In Belfast, Cara, 11, reads her sister Orla's messages on the shared iPad.» Here iPad names one particular tablet.
explain: iPad is a brand name, so it starts with a capital letter and belongs to one company's product. Many tablets are made by other companies, so they are not iPads. Check the clues: a touch screen, no keyboard, made by Apple means it is an iPad.
fact: An iPad is a tablet computer made by Apple.
fact: An iPad has a touch screen and no keyboard.
fact: Pupils use iPads at school for reading, maths games, photos and research.
fact: «Posts offering free iPads or prizes for sharing and clicking are usually scams.»
fact: Scams try to collect your personal details or spread harmful links, so never click them and tell an adult.
exercise: «In Belfast, Cara, 11, reads her sister Orla's messages on the shared iPad.» What kind of thing is an iPad? | *A tablet computer | A pet | A bus ticket | A type of food
exercise: Why does iPad start with a capital letter? | Every word in a sentence needs a capital | Computers always need capitals | Days of the week need capitals | *It is a brand name, the name of one company's product
exercise: Which thing does an iPad NOT have? | Maths games | *A keyboard | A touch screen | Photos
test: Which is a school use of an iPad? | Cooking dinner | Filling a bath | Mowing the lawn | *Reading and maths games
test: «Posts offering free iPads for clicking are usually...» What is the right ending? | *Scams | Free to click | Safe to share with friends | Prizes from Apple
exam: A post offers a free iPad if you click a link. What should you do? | Click it quickly before the offer ends | Type your address into the form | Share it with all your friends | *Never click it, and tell an adult
